# Sub-processor disclosure rule

The Privacy Policy at `src/pages/Privacy.tsx` discloses a fixed list of
sub-processors that handle customer data on our behalf:

- Stripe (payment processing)
- Vercel (hosting)
- Supabase (database)
- USPS and UPS (shipping carriers)

**If you add ANY new third-party service that processes customer personal
data, you MUST also update the Privacy Policy's "Who we share it with
(sub-processors)" section in the same change.** This includes (but is
not limited to):

- SMS marketing providers (Twilio, Postscript, Klaviyo SMS, etc.)
- Email marketing providers (Klaviyo, Mailchimp, ConvertKit, SendGrid,
  Postmark, Customer.io, etc.)
- Transactional email senders (Resend, SES, Postmark, etc.)
- Analytics tools (Google Analytics, GA4, Plausible, PostHog, Mixpanel,
  Heap, Amplitude, Hotjar, FullStory, session-replay, etc.)
- Ad / tracking pixels (Meta, TikTok, Google Ads, Reddit, etc.) — **and
  if you do add one of these, also remove the line in Privacy that says
  "we do not set advertising cookies, retargeting pixels, or third-party
  tracking pixels"**.
- CRM / helpdesk (Intercom, Zendesk, HubSpot, Crisp, etc.)
- Reviews / UGC platforms (Yotpo, Okendo, Trustpilot, etc.)
- Loyalty / rewards platforms (Smile.io, LoyaltyLion, etc.)
- Affiliate networks (Refersion, Impact, etc.)
- Sub-processors used by Supabase or Vercel that materially expand
  data-sharing (e.g. enabling Vercel Analytics, Supabase Edge Functions
  with third-party APIs).

The rule is one-way: adding a service requires updating Privacy.
Removing a service should also remove its sub-processor listing.

If a campaign or integration is added without updating Privacy, the
policy becomes materially false and exposes Percival LLC to consumer-
protection claims. Do not skip this step.

## How to add a sub-processor entry

Edit the `<ul>` inside the "Who we share it with (sub-processors)"
section in `src/pages/Privacy.tsx`. Each entry follows the pattern:

```tsx
<li>
  <strong>Provider Name</strong> &mdash; one-line description of what
  the provider does and what data it receives.
</li>
```

Keep the descriptions concise and accurate. Don't add a provider
unless it is actually wired up in production.

## Marketing-tool specific

When wiring up an email or SMS marketing tool:

1. Add the provider to the sub-processor list as above.
2. Make sure the account-creation marketing-opt-in checkboxes (per
   Privacy "Marketing communications" section) actually persist to and
   sync with the new provider.
3. Implement the unsubscribe / STOP-reply flow before launching the
   first campaign.
4. Document the provider and the data fields synced in
   `business-policies.mdc` under "Marketing communications".
